From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Connor Prussin <connor@prussin.net>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a pointer theme still loading is no error

On every start the desk's pointer theme loads off the UI thread, so the
first cursors are Chromium's art and this line fired at ERROR each time.
The DRM cursor factory already says at ERROR when a theme is missing or
lacks a type, so this one is VERBOSE.
---
 ui/wm/core/cursor_loader.cc | 13 ++++++-------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ui/wm/core/cursor_loader.cc b/ui/wm/core/cursor_loader.cc
index 2237553..ef93304 100644
--- a/ui/wm/core/cursor_loader.cc
+++ b/ui/wm/core/cursor_loader.cc
@@ -216,13 +216,12 @@ scoped_refptr<ui::PlatformCursor> CursorLoader::CursorFromType(
     // The cursor may fail to load if the cursor theme has just been reset.
     // We will be notified when the theme is loaded, but at this time we have to
     // fall back to the assets.
-    // Domicile: at ERROR, the level the engine logs at, so a pointer that is
-    // Chromium's art says so. Once per type until the cursors unload. kNull,
-    // "no cursor set", has no name in a cursor theme and is always Chromium's
-    // pointer, so it is no error.
-    LOG_IF(ERROR, type != CursorType::kNull)
-        << "domicile: the pointer's " << type << " cursor at scale " << scale_
-        << " is Chromium's: the platform has none";
+    // Domicile: why the pointer is Chromium's art, once per type until the
+    // cursors unload. A theme still loading, as on every start, lands here
+    // too, so it is no error: the platform's cursor factory says at ERROR
+    // when a theme is missing or lacks a type.
+    VLOG(1) << "domicile: the pointer's " << type << " cursor at scale "
+            << scale_ << " is Chromium's: the platform has none";
   }
 
   // Loads the default Aura cursor bitmap for the cursor type. Falls back on
